Romania on Wednesday was probing a possible fresh drone attack on a tanker off its Black Sea coast. Suspected Russian drones have hit several ships off Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria since last week in the latest spillover from the Ukraine war in the Black Sea. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ec22678-c84a-11f1-85e1-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6L73WH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ec22678-c84a-11f1-85e1-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6L73WH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2419a9ac-c81a-11f1-9243-6b277543ded8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:52:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3ec22678-c84a-11f1-85e1-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6L73WH.jpg">© Daniel Mihailescu, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Albania protests turn violent as protestors demand PM Rama's resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation</link><description>
Anti-government protests in Albania’s capital Tirana turned violent for a second consecutive night on Wednesday, leaving several government buildings damaged and at least one ablaze. Thousands demanded Prime Minister Edi Rama’s resignation and improved university conditions. Police fired tear gas and deployed water cannons as protesters smashed windows and attacked buildings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b967b1f4-c81d-11f1-a7c2-d51d50e7e553</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:35:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fbf524c2-c820-11f1-9100-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T222222Z-1949817444-RC233OAJSBMG-RTRMADP-3-ALBANIA-PROTESTS.jpg">© Florion Goga, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261014-french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting</link><description>
The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc2a50c6-c810-11f1-ba96-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-223114-224215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc2a50c6-c810-11f1-ba96-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-223114-224215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a73b45e-c812-11f1-9191-3db5c6d9150e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:01:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting</link><description>
The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc2a50c6-c810-11f1-ba96-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-223114-224215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc2a50c6-c810-11f1-ba96-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-223114-224215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01338ce0-c811-11f1-bf27-b3491a10e8e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What is Starshield, SpaceX's military version of Starlink?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink</link><description>
Elon Musk’s ⁠SpaceX restricted “military-grade” ​Starlink services overnight into Wednesday, hampering Ukrainian drone strike missions and air defenses, Ukraine reported. In response, Musk said that the US government was behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9675ed00-c809-11f1-8cec-2b55fa072aed</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:15:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6d59c4e-c807-11f1-a293-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/Starshield.jpg">© ZUMA Press Wire via Reuters Connect, Gene Blevins</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing</link><description>
Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9680d490-c804-11f1-9a9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-211506-211649-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b9d2a14-c804-11f1-9cd4-bd6088dee01f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:56:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres</link><description>
Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7652471c-c804-11f1-ac63-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-210507-211251-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b7c5e62-c804-11f1-98f3-2dea6aa53833</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:49:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions</link><description>
Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b26d3c6-c7ac-11f1-967a-c1ef70811b87</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:14:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dc465e0-c7ab-11f1-8b0a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D38A7G3.jpg">© Yasuyoshi Chiba, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump says 'massive' oil, gas and mineral exploration to begin in Greenland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said on Wednesday that a "massive" oil, gas and mineral exploration was slated to begin in Greenland. The US, Denmark and Greenland last month signed a security agreement after Trump's repeated threats to seize control of the island.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07b7b4b6-c798-11f1-9f35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HN7ZP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07b7b4b6-c798-11f1-9f35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HN7ZP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5de06ad4-c795-11f1-a316-2f61a496b220</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:41:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07b7b4b6-c798-11f1-9f35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7HN7ZP.jpg">© Mads Claus Rasmussen, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trial lawyer for Ukrainian accused of sabotage says Russia used Nord Stream as a ‘weapon’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-defence-of-ukrainian-accused-of-sabotage-says-russia-used-nord-stream-pipelines-as-weapon</link><description>
The Nord Stream gas pipelines were a political and economic “weapon” for Russia, the lawyer for former Ukrainian officer Sergei Kuznetsov said Wednesday. The first to appear in the high-profile case, Kuznetsov is accused by German prosecutors of having led the plan to sabotage the infrastructure in 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9df5c22-c7b5-11f1-91c8-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/29c7a146c259ea0035165420779e79abf67094b2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9df5c22-c7b5-11f1-91c8-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/29c7a146c259ea0035165420779e79abf67094b2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2157252-c799-11f1-8bbf-99df71945f85</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:37:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9df5c22-c7b5-11f1-91c8-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/29c7a146c259ea0035165420779e79abf67094b2.jpg">© Markus Scholz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US government behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system, Musk says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead</link><description>
SpaceX boss Elon Musk said Wednesday that any disruptions in the Starshield satellite communications system would be the responsibility of the US government, not his company. Earlier, Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelensky called on Musk to “switch on” the system which Kyiv relies on for communications and logistics. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b758477e-c80a-11f1-a128-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Starlink.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b758477e-c80a-11f1-a128-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Starlink.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0eb01c3e-c795-11f1-8077-7dfe2a3dae99</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:19:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b758477e-c80a-11f1-a128-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Starlink.jpg">© Yasuyoshi Chiba, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What we know about Pope Leo XIV's lung cancer diagnosis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation</link><description>
Pope Leo underwent surgery on Tuesday to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung after saying that a nodule had been "detected at a very early stage". Following a "successful" operation, the Vatican said the 71-year-old pontiff would undergo additional testing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53f3f2bc-c780-11f1-8b9b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/bc5297502224d0f6c9b874b9e105367eca367671.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53f3f2bc-c780-11f1-8b9b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/bc5297502224d0f6c9b874b9e105367eca367671.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54e53f1e-c780-11f1-a057-a1f98f7801ef</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:35:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53f3f2bc-c780-11f1-8b9b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/bc5297502224d0f6c9b874b9e105367eca367671.jpg">© Andreas Solaro, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Kyiv power plant hit by Russian missile without warning from allies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that a Russian ballistic missile struck a Kyiv power plant without advance warning from Western allies, killing at least two people and wounding around 20. The attack came days after US President Donald Trump announced an energy ceasefire between Moscow and Kyiv, raising questions over efforts to halt strikes on critical infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fae67824-c767-11f1-bb13-c5a9b4bd2820</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:41:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo has cancerous growth removed in lung operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV had a cancerous growth removed from his right lung in a 90-minute operation on Tuesday and "woke up normally" after the procedure, the Vatican said. A Vatican source said further tests were being carried out to determine if the cancer had spread. "To ensure the procedure was radical, the lower lobe of the right lung was removed," the Vatican said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16231fa6-c74b-11f1-a4f0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-230330-230812-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16231fa6-c74b-11f1-a4f0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-230330-230812-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b51ea8e-c74b-11f1-aa5e-db1448cc4d3c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:23:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Have Ukrainian strikes on Yandex data centres hit Russian online disinformation?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261013-have-ukrainian-strikes-on-yandex-data-centres-hit-russian-online-disinformation</link><description>
After recent Ukrainian bombings of Russian data centres belonging to Yandex, internet users claim to have noticed a sharp reduction in pro-Russian and far-right populist social media content. They suggest the reduction is a direct result of the strikes cutting off Russian disinformation "bots". We examine the claim in this edition of Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbb9828c-c7af-11f1-9c4a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6a006bff.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbb9828c-c7af-11f1-9c4a-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6a006bff.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdeb269c-c748-11f1-b5d1-03d80f31c1e9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:59:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emerald MAXWELL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit</link><description>
King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd4d9a70-c737-11f1-948a-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-203549-204111-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd4d9a70-c737-11f1-948a-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-203549-204111-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3170b12-c737-11f1-aa53-d798fadc02e5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:06:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>King Felipe VI says Ceuta is ‘inalienable’ part of Spain in landmark visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx</link><description>
King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta on Tuesday for the first time in 14 years, with the monarch reaffirming Spain’s sovereignty over the North African enclaves claimed by Morocco. The landmark visit comes amid strained relations with Rabat and the aftermath of a mass migrant influx that saw makeshift camps cleared ahead of the royals’ arrival.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed7deb02-c714-11f1-8a12-33956213bea6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:17:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg">© Manu Fernandez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgium: Greener schools thanks to European funding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding</link><description>
🇧🇪 In Ganshoren, in Belgium, a new school replaces run-down buildings. But the need for renovations remains enormous.👉🏻 Find the whole reporting on France 24 English. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95428516-c70e-11f1-80b7-914b699b402e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:27:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia pounds Ukrainian cities, spares energy targets for first time since Trump 'ceasefire'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire</link><description>
Russia hammered Ukrainian cities and transport links overnight into Tuesday, killing at least four people in the city of Kharkiv, while appearing to spare energy facilities for the first time since US President Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire" at the weekend. It was not clear whether Moscow had deliberately avoided targeting power plants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8171a586-c703-11f1-9a3d-3b1e1fb2f193</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:39:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg">© Sofiia Gatilova, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish royals visit crisis-hit Ceuta amid diplomatic tensions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions</link><description>
Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time since 2007, amid tensions with Morocco following July’s migration crisis, when more than 70,000 people crossed into the Spanish enclave. Most returned to Morocco, but thousands remained, and dozens died. Morocco claims sovereignty over Ceuta, making the royal visit diplomatically sensitive. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris has more from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97223c96-c704-11f1-ad22-ff6afdbff2d2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Transactional diplomacy': Greece positioning itself as Trump's most 'reliable ally in the region'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-region</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Petros Konstantinidis, a financial journalist for Greece's leading daily newspaper TA NEA. The current controversy surrounding the US ambassador to Greece, Kimberly Guilfoyle, has all the makings of a reality TV show or a telenovela, or both. "This is diplomacy under Trump turning into lifestyle diplomacy," Konstantinidis explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832a9522-c71c-11f1-b142-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-41d692d4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832a9522-c71c-11f1-b142-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-41d692d4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">147ed8ca-c6fb-11f1-b2d6-55ed6e285468</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:41:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain’s king visits Ceuta amid tensions with Morocco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco</link><description>
King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia are visiting Ceuta months after more than 70,000 migrants arrived from Morocco. While most have returned, thousands remain. The visit has divided residents and risks reigniting diplomatic tensions with Morocco, which claims sovereignty over Ceuta and Melilla.
